    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW28UERLEmTEMKHTp9uJhsWYe)_\n\n## What\n`.config/emacs-modular/README.org` and `docs/main.org` had the same purpose, so they are now one document: **`README.org`** at the top of `.config/emacs-modular` (as requested), and `docs/main.org` is removed.\n\n- `README.org` is the old `docs/main.org` (history kept by `git mv`) with the README's introduction and the \"Testing a pull request in a sandbox\" section added. Its relative links were rewritten for the new location (`docs/...`, `libraries/...`).\n- The tangling how-to moved to the new `docs/tangling-instructions.org`, linked from `README.org`.\n\n## References updated\n- The \"To tangle, see ...\" line in the 130 module docs links `docs/tangling-instructions.org`.\n- `sp-sandbox` (doc and `.el` commentary), the `sp-org-agenda` doc, `docs/architecture/load-order.org`, and a few mentions of `main.org` in other docs now say `README.org`.\n- `sp-typst`: the book's Overview is now just `README.org`, and \"Design notes\" no longer needs to exclude `docs/main.org`; doc and `.el` kept in sync.\n- CHANGELOG entry added; older entries that mention `docs/main.org` are history and unchanged.\n\n## Not tested\nNo Emacs in the container: nothing was tangled, byte-compiled or run. The `.el` edits are one comment and the `sp-typst--parts` list/`remove` call. Please check that the Org links resolve (`C-c C-o`) and that the typst book still builds.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi98SJti3bzDUzFYHJR",
